    "num": "Chapter VIII",
    "title": "Credits & GPA",
    "url": "credits-gpa.html",
    "desc": "An interactive breakdown of graduation requisites, mark distributions, course grading tables, and our live GPA estimator tool.",
    "content": "Chapter VIII: Credits &amp; GPA | PES University Handbook ✕ Chapter VIII Credits &amp; GPA \"Academic progress is measured in credit weights, structured assessments, and index calculations. Remember, GPA is important, but isn't everything; students can always recover in subsequent semesters and still achieve excellent results in placements.\" ALGORITHMIC ENGINES SGPA CALCULATOR • CREDIT SYSTEM REGULATIONS The Credit Structure 💡 Credits are simply defined as the weightage given to a particular subject. One of the first academic terms you'll hear at PESU is credits. Every course you complete carries a certain number of credits, and these credits, along with your grades, determine your academic progress and GPA. To successfully complete your undergraduate programme, you'll need to earn 160 credits . Most courses are assigned one of the following credit values: 5, 4, or 2 . Generally, lab courses carry higher credits, while other subjects may have lower credit values. How Do You Earn Credits? You earn the entire credit value of a course only if you pass it by securing a grade between S and E. If you receive an F grade, you do not earn any credits for that course (it is an all-or-nothing system). You'll need to clear the course in a future semester to earn those credits. GPA Index Equations \\[SGPA = \\frac{\\sum (C_i \\times G_i)}{\\sum C_i}\\] Where \\(C_i\\) represents course credits and \\(G_i\\) is the grade point obtained. CGPA = Average of SGPA values Where CGPA is calculated simply as the average of all your semester SGPA scores. Marks &amp; Grades Distribution Each course is evaluated using both internal and external assessments. Weightage is split: Internal Assessment (50 marks) + End Semester Assessment (50 marks) = 100 Marks . Internal Assessment Components (50M) ISA 1: 40 Marks scaled down to 20 Marks ISA 2: 40 Marks scaled down to 20 Marks Assignments / Continuous Assessment: 10 Marks External Assessment (50M) The ESA is conducted for 100 marks, but the score is scaled down to 50 marks before being combined with your internal marks. Final Marks = Internal (50) + Scaled ESA (50) 🧪 Lab-Integrated Courses Some subjects are lab-integrated courses where both theory and laboratory components contribute. Marks: ISA + Assignments (Internal) 50, ESA (Theory) 100, Laboratory Component 20, Total Raw Marks 120. Grade Meaning Marks Range Grade Point S Outstanding 90–100 10 A Excellent 80–89 9 B Very Good 70–79 8 C Good 60–69 7 D Fair 50–59 6 E Satisfactory 40–49 5 F Fail 0–39 4 W Withdrawn — 0 AP Audit Pass 40–100 0 AF Audit Fail 0–39 0 Note: Although an F grade has a point value of 4 in the grading table, it is a failed course. It does not earn credits and negatively impacts your GPA. Grade Calculation Examples 1. Subject without lab: ISA = 35/40, ESA = 82/100, Assignment = 10/10 \\[\\text{ISA} + \\left(\\frac{\\text{ESA}}{2}\\right) + \\text{Assignment} = 35 + 41 + 10 = \\frac{86}{100}\\] 2. Subject with lab: ISA = 35/40, ESA = 82/100, Assignment = 10/10, Lab = 18/20 \\[\\text{Final Score} = \\left(\\frac{\\text{ESA} + \\text{Lab}}{120} \\times 50\\right) + \\text{ISA} + \\text{Assignments}\\] \\[\\text{Final Score} = \\left(\\frac{82 + 18}{120} \\times 50\\right) + 35 + 10 = 86.67\\] Understanding Subject Codes Every subject at PES University follows a structured subject code: UE JY SC Y C N A/B • UE: Undergraduate Engineering • JY: Year of Admission (e.g. 26 = 2026 Batch) • SC: Subject Category (e.g., CS, EC, ME, CY, PH, MA) • Y: Year of Study (1 = 1st Year, 2 = 2nd Year, etc.) • C: Number of Credits • N: Serial Number of the Subject within that credit category • A / B: Semester Code (A = Odd Semester, B = Even Semester) • Example: UE26CY151A represents: Undergraduate Eng., 2026 Batch, Chemistry, 1st Year, 5-credit, 1st subject, Odd Semester. Interactive GPA Estimator Physics Cycle Chemistry Cycle Estimated SGPA 9.00 Real-time projection based on credits. Note: If the Chemistry Cycle is your first cycle, please assume Math II to be Math I, and Problem Solving with C to be Problem Solving with Python for the purpose of calculator entries. READ SPEED --- WPM COMPLETED: 0%"
